// ============================================================================
// Secrets.example.xcconfig — committed template
// ============================================================================
// Copy this file to `Secrets.xcconfig` in the same folder and fill in the two
// values. `Secrets.xcconfig` is gitignored.
//
//     cp nyc-tracker/Config/Secrets.example.xcconfig nyc-tracker/Config/Secrets.xcconfig
//
// Then point the project at it: Xcode → project (blue icon) → Info →
// Configurations → set both Debug and Release to `Secrets`.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// IMPORTANT: the host, not the full URL
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// .xcconfig treats `//` as the start of a comment, so this:
//
//     SUPABASE_URL = https://abcdefghijkl.supabase.co
//
// silently becomes `https:` and the app fails at launch with a useless error.
// That's why the setting below is the bare HOST with no scheme. SupabaseConfig
// prepends `https://` in Swift, where the problem doesn't exist.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// Project host — Supabase Dashboard → Settings → API Keys (or Data API) →
// Project URL, with the leading `https://` removed.
// Example: abcdefghijklmnop.supabase.co
SUPABASE_PROJECT_HOST = iirdvkwjrycuplokouhn.supabase.co

// Publishable key — Supabase Dashboard → Settings → API Keys → "Publishable key".
// Starts with `sb_publishable_`.
//
// This replaced the legacy `anon` JWT key. Projects created recently have no
// legacy keys at all, so if you're looking for "Project API keys → anon public"
// you're reading stale instructions — that section no longer exists.
//
// Safe to ship in a client binary: it carries no privilege of its own and every
// table is protected by RLS.
//
// NEVER put a `sb_secret_...` value here. That is the secret key (the old
// `service_role`), it has BYPASSRLS, and anything in this file ends up inside the
// app bundle where it can be extracted. The two names are one word apart and
// `sb_secret_` looks harmless next to `sb_publishable_` — check the prefix before
// you paste.
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY = sb_publishable_xlEUgrWmIr86Wkj_waiEiQ_XrkVThHi